            "id": "314408962",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P2 · Storage Degrading While Running Out Of Space — CONFIRMED\n**WHAT:** Either signal alone is routine: volumes get slow under load, and volumes fill up predictably. Together on the SAME device they mean the filesystem is degrading as it approaches its limit, which is how a slow disk becomes a stopped service.\n**WHY THIS IS DIFFERENT:** every member condition below is true at the same time, which is what separates a real incident from an isolated symptom:\n  - Storage Latency Anomaly\n  - Disk Exhaustion Forecast\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod`\n**SERVICE / SCOPE:** `compute-platform` (infrastructure)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Confirmed impact: every member condition is true simultaneously, which is the evidence threshold this platform requires before paging on a symptom.\n**OWNER:** infrastructure-engineering · pages the on-call rotation\n**DO THIS NEXT:** Treat as a confirmed incident. The member alerts are the evidence trail; the runbook's remediation section applies directly.\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Disk Exhaustion Forecast` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-host`.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-infra-compute-availability`\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Storage Degrading While Running Out Of Space\nAt least one member condition cleared, so the confirmed-impact state no longer holds. Individual member monitors may still be alerting — check before closing the incident.\n{{/is_recovery}}",
