        {
          "index_key": "custom.prod.checkout-payment-latency",
          "schema_version": 0,
          "attributes": {
            "assets": [
              {
                "category": "runbook",
                "name": "API p99 Latency Degradation",
                "resource_key": "15298349",
                "resource_type": "notebook",
                "url": "https://app.datadoghq.com/notebook/15298349"
              }
            ],
            "draft_status": "published",
            "enable_logs_sample": null,
            "enable_samples": null,
            "escalation_message": "",
            "evaluation_delay": 300,
            "force_delete": null,
            "group_retention_duration": "",
            "groupby_simple_monitor": null,
            "id": "314408862",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P2 · Checkout Payment Latency\n**WHAT:** checkout-payment-latency: custom monitor requested by payments.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `checkout-api` (api / service, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Service-specific impact declared by the owning team; see the runbook.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The platform pack applies api-latency-p99 (rate-of-change) to every API. Checkout has a strong weekly traffic shape — Monday morning and Friday evening peaks are 4x the trough — so rate-of-change produces recurring false positives at the shoulders of each peak. `predictive.anomaly: true` selects the seasonal variant (robust/weekly) for THIS service only, which learns the shape instead of reacting to it. The pack monitor stays in place for every other API.\n\n**OWNER:** payments · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `API p99 Latency Degradation` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-api-health` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `api-services.prod.checkout-api` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-api-latency` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Checkout Payment Latency — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P2.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Checkout Payment Latency — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Checkout Payment Latency\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-api-latency`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "1",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P2][prod][api] Checkout Payment Latency (critical)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "2",
            "query": "avg(last_30m):anomalies(p95:trace.http.request.duration{env:prod,service:checkout-api} by {service}, 'robust', 3, direction='above', seasonality='weekly') \u003e= 1",
            "renotify_interval": 30,
            "renotify_occurrences": 3,
            "renotify_statuses": [
