            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Scheduled Job Did Not Run\n**WHAT:** Scheduled Job Did Not Run: schedule_miss signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `integration-platform` (integration / scheduled_job, tier3)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Customers are affected now, or a mission-critical capability is unavailable.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The single most under-monitored failure in every enterprise: the job that simply never fired. Nothing errors, nothing alerts, nothing runs.\n\n**OWNER:** application-development · support best-effort · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Scheduled Job Did Not Run` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `remediate-rerun-job` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `scheduler.prod.integration-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-integration-delivery` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Scheduled Job Did Not Run — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Scheduled Job Did Not Run — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Scheduled Job Did Not Run\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-integration-delivery`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "1",
