            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Workload Memory Saturation Forecast\n**WHAT:** Workload Memory Saturation Forecast: saturation signal detected by forecast analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `kubernetes-platform` (kubernetes / kube_deployment, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Extrapolating the recent trend, this resource is projected to cross its limit inside the forecast horizon. It has not crossed it yet — that is the point.\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Workload Memory Saturation Forecast` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `remediate-scale-workload` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `kubernetes-workloads.prod.kubernetes-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-k8s-workload-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Workload Memory Saturation Forecast — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Workload Memory Saturation Forecast — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Workload Memory Saturation Forecast\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-k8s-workload-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
