            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P2 · Platform Deployment Pipeline Failing\n**WHAT:** Platform Deployment Pipeline Failing: job_failure signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `platform-services` (platform / pipeline, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Two consecutive pipeline failures separates a flaky run from a broken deployment path.\n\n**OWNER:** observability-platform · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Platform Deployment Pipeline Failing` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-ticket-sustained` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `ci-cd.prod.platform-services` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-platform-services` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Platform Deployment Pipeline Failing — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P2.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Platform Deployment Pipeline Failing — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Platform Deployment Pipeline Failing\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-platform-services`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
