            "id": "314408640",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P1 · Telemetry Ingest Pipeline Degraded\n**WHAT:** A 40% collapse in custom-metric ingest means a large part of the estate has gone dark. This is the highest-leverage monitor in the repository: it is what stops \"all green\" from meaning \"all blind\".\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `platform-services` (platform / monitoring_platform, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Customers are affected now, or a mission-critical capability is unavailable.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The signal changed faster than the configured percentage relative to its own recent history. Speed of degradation, not absolute level.\n**OWNER:** observability-platform · support 24x7 · this pages the on-call rotation\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Telemetry Ingest Pipeline Degraded` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-major-incident` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `observability-platform.prod.platform-services` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-platform-services` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Telemetry Ingest Pipeline Degraded — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P1.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Telemetry Ingest Pipeline Degraded — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Telemetry Ingest Pipeline Degraded\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-platform-services`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "-40",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "-20",
