            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Batch Job Duration Anomaly\n**WHAT:** The earliest reliable warning that tonight's batch will miss its window — hours before the missed-completion monitor would fire.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `batch-platform` (integration / batch_job, tier2)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** The signal deviated from its learned SEASONAL baseline (same hour, same day of week), so normal daily and weekly cycles are already accounted for.\n**OWNER:** application-development · support business-hours · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Batch Job Duration Anomaly` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-batch-job` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `batch-platform.prod.batch-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-batch-completion` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Batch Job Duration Anomaly — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Batch Job Duration Anomaly — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Batch Job Duration Anomaly\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-batch-completion`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
