            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Endpoint TLS Certificate Approaching Expiry\n**WHAT:** Endpoint TLS Certificate Approaching Expiry: certificate_expiry signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `external-dependencies` (saas / synthetic_check, tier2)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** 21 days matches the PKI renewal lead time.\n**OWNER:** sre · support business-hours · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Endpoint TLS Certificate Approaching Expiry` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-cert-renewal-ticket` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `external-endpoint.prod.external-dependencies` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-external-dependency` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Endpoint TLS Certificate Approaching Expiry — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Endpoint TLS Certificate Approaching Expiry — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Endpoint TLS Certificate Approaching Expiry\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-external-dependency`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
