            "id": "314408690",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Datastore Capacity Exhaustion Forecast\n**WHAT:** A full datastore stops every VM on it simultaneously. One week of lead time reflects the storage team's provisioning cycle.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `virtualization-platform` (vmware / vsphere_datastore, tier2)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Extrapolating the recent trend, this resource is projected to cross its limit inside the forecast horizon. It has not crossed it yet — that is the point.\n**OWNER:** infrastructure-engineering · support business-hours · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `Datastore Capacity Exhaustion Forecast` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-capacity-ticket` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `datastore.prod.virtualization-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-vmware-cluster-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Datastore Capacity Exhaustion Forecast — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Datastore Capacity Exhaustion Forecast — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Datastore Capacity Exhaustion Forecast\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-vmware-cluster-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "0.9",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "0.85",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P3][prod][vmware] Datastore Capacity Exhaustion Forecast (standard)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "3",
            "query": "max(next_1w):forecast(avg:vsphere.datastore.disk.used{env:prod,alert_band:standard} by {vsphere_datastore} / avg:vsphere.datastore.disk.capacity{env:prod,alert_band:standard} by {vsphere_datastore}, 'linear', 1, interval='60m', history='2w') \u003e 0.9",
