        {
          "index_key": "prod.standard.vmware.vmware-snapshot-age",
          "schema_version": 0,
          "attributes": {
            "assets": [
              {
                "category": "runbook",
                "name": "VM Snapshot Older Than Policy",
                "resource_key": "15298702",
                "resource_type": "notebook",
                "url": "https://app.datadoghq.com/notebook/15298702"
              }
            ],
            "draft_status": "published",
            "enable_logs_sample": null,
            "enable_samples": null,
            "escalation_message": "",
            "evaluation_delay": 300,
            "force_delete": null,
            "group_retention_duration": "",
            "groupby_simple_monitor": null,
            "id": "314408706",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P4 · VM Snapshot Older Than Policy\n**WHAT:** VM Snapshot Older Than Policy: capacity signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `virtualization-platform` (vmware / vsphere_vm, tier2)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Observability or configuration hygiene is degraded. No direct customer impact, but our ability to see or govern the estate is reduced.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Seven days is the operational policy limit; aged snapshots consume datastore capacity and slow consolidation unpredictably.\n\n**OWNER:** infrastructure-engineering · support business-hours · this does not page\n**RUNBOOK:** attached to this monitor as `VM Snapshot Older Than Policy` — open it from the monitor's Runbook asset.\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-capacity-ticket` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `datastore.prod.virtualization-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-vmware-cluster-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## VM Snapshot Older Than Policy — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P4.\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## VM Snapshot Older Than Policy — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one.\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · VM Snapshot Older Than Policy\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-vmware-cluster-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "7",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "3",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P4][prod][vmware] VM Snapshot Older Than Policy (standard)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [
              "vsphere_cluster"
            ],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "4",
            "query": "max(last_6h):max:acme.vmware.snapshot_age_days{env:prod,alert_band:standard} by {vsphere_cluster,vm_name} \u003e 7",
            "renotify_interval": 120,
            "renotify_occurrences": 3,
            "renotify_statuses": [
